# Docker build context = repository ROOT for the CANONICAL image (build: `docker
# build -f apps/backend/Dockerfile.canonical .`). That image COPYs exactly
# apps/backend/ plus the one committed catalog file
# (packages/contracts/commercial-catalog.v1.json); nothing else is ever added to an
# image layer. This denylist keeps the context small and — critically — guarantees
# that no local secret, database, or dev artifact under apps/backend can be baked
# into the image via `COPY apps/backend`. (The backend-context apps/backend/Dockerfile
# used by Railway staging builds from apps/backend/ and does not read this file.)
#
# Safety invariant: NOTHING here may exclude apps/backend/** or
# packages/contracts/commercial-catalog.v1.json — those are what the image needs.

# Version control + CI metadata (large; never needed inside the image).
.git
.github

# Python bytecode / tool caches.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Virtualenvs (never ship a host venv into the image).
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Local environment files and secrets — must never be baked in.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# SQLite databases and their WAL/SHM sidecars. Production data lives ONLY on the
# /data persistent disk; a dev database must never enter the image.
**/*.db
**/*.db-*

# Large sibling trees outside the backend image build context.
apps/android
apps/ios
apps/web
artifacts
build
docs
schema
supabase
vendor
**/node_modules/
